      "writtenOn": "2023-07-14T21:42:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe it would be problematic when the base module does not set the `a.stem` property.\nFor instance:\n```\nandroid_app {\n    name: \"foo\",\n    srcs: [\"a.java\"],\n    sdk_version: \"current\",\n}\n\noverride_android_app {\n    name: \"bar\",\n    base: \"foo\",\n}\n```\nIn the above example, `bar.stem` is expected to be `foo`, not `bar`. However, `bar.installApkPath` is expected to be `bar.java`, not `foo.java`. Therefore, due to the difference in the expected behavior or `stem` and `installApkName`, I believe that the property of the two cannot be shared.\n\nI\u0027ve added documentation for `a.stem`.",
      "parentUuid": "5cbcfb20_726079ef",
      "revId": "a5b120252a3f181921139008d3643de74017d424",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
